Environment: Windows 11 Pro (10.0.26200), go1.26.6 windows/amd64, git-bash shell.
Per Makefile/docs/dev-environment.md: build, vet and test are expected to work
from a Windows checkout even though real observation needs Linux. Verified here.

$ gofmt -l ./cmd ./internal
(no output - nothing needs formatting)
exit: 0

$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go vet ./...
(no output - clean)
exit: 0

$ CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go vet ./...
(no output - clean)
exit: 0

$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./...
ok  	github.com/OmarAlghafri/netrewind/cmd/netrewind	2.146s
