$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o build/netrewindd.exe ./cmd/netrewindd
$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o build/netrewind.exe ./cmd/netrewind
BUILD OK

$ ./build/netrewind.exe version
netrewind dev (schema v1)

$ ./build/netrewind.exe --help
NetRewind records what changed on the network so it can be replayed after the fact.

Usage:
  netrewind [command]

Available Commands:
  completion    Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  events        List recorded events in time order
  help          Help about any command
  incidents     List what correlation concluded, with the chain behind each conclusion
  rules         Load and check the correlation rules
  serve         Read the record in a browser
  timeline      Read recorded history as a narrative
  version       Print the version
  what-happened Reconstruct what happened around a moment, for one machine or for all of them

Flags:
      --db string   path to the event store
  -h, --help        help for netrewind

Result: build, vet (native + linux target) and the full test suite are all
clean on native Windows, and the CLI binary runs. This matches what the
project documents ("build, vet, test... work from a Windows or macOS
checkout too") and is the cross-platform half of the baseline.
